            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a move (in a game), then the Urdu for to turn over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بساط",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بساط — bisāt — \"a game board\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر بساط ہے تو ہم شطرنج کھیلیں گے۔ agar bisāt hai to ham shatranj kheleṅ ge. If you have a board, we'll play chess."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بساط (bisāt) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic bisāṭ, \"a carpet, something spread out\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
